sink|PASS: A stone moving below water matches chìm and the source verb; sank is correctly used with sunk reserved as the participle. The transitive ship construction is a grammar extension of sinking, not an unsupported sink-container noun.
wall|PASS: Upright enclosing/dividing/supporting structure fits a classroom wall. Vietnamese preserves beside the door and attached map. On versus against is a useful spatial distinction, with no fabricated building dimension.
aspect|PASS: Financial feature of opening a library is a discrete aspect, not an appearance or grammatical-aspect proposal. Khía cạnh and of-complement are accurate. The example remains fictional and makes no actual budget claim.
glad|PASS: Glad to hear uses the normal predicative infinitive construction. Vietnamese retains that the missing dog returned. The warning about attributive glad is qualified as ordinary description, avoiding an absolute ban on literary uses.
key|PASS: Lock tool, essential adjective, keyboard input verb, keyboard button and means-to-success noun represent five genuinely different grammatical/semantic boundaries. Vietnamese differentiates chìa khóa, quan trọng, nhập, phím and bí quyết. Keyed and key to improving are correct; no instrument or musical-key sense is inferred.
